A chapter title / subtitle, focused
description: the chapter_title_editing state
- >
  The document's (or a subchapter's) self-value as an editable heading, or the keyed `description`
  as the subtitle - the SAME editor at every level, indented. Title and description are OPTIONAL
  and have NO placeholder cells - a cell exists only when its model does; any one-line chunk takes
  (or gives back) the role via the bar's T / D buttons. Opening the editor lands in the first cell
  that EXISTS - title, description, first paragraph, or an empty chapter's bootstrap paragraph. A
  title EMPTIED character by character drops its self line and the caret lands on the chapter's
  first remaining stop (never nowhere - the reported lost focus)
- !!<*yamlover: $defs: table>
  header:
    - Event
      width: 2
    - 'Condition / note'
      width: 4
    - 'Next state'
      width: 2
  - ['`enter`', 'at the START of a non-empty subchapter title - the word-processor push-down: an empty paragraph opens BEFORE the whole subchapter', '[chapter_prose_editing](*::server:chapter-editor:chapter_prose_editing)']
  - ['`enter`', 'the first body chunk is a SUBCHAPTER heading or an ATOM - the walk would land on something untypeable, so an empty paragraph opens as the FIRST chunk instead (insertHead)', '[chapter_prose_editing](*::server:chapter-editor:chapter_prose_editing)']
  - ['`enter`', 'otherwise - the walk: title → description → the body (a first paragraph is made if none)', '`chapter_title_editing` (stays)']
  - ['`ctrl_enter`', 'THE TABLE GESTURE - the titled block becomes a table (the bar''s ▦)', '[format_switched](*::server:chapter-editor:format_switched)']
  - ['`tab`', 'a title whose PREVIOUS sibling is a chapter AND the subtree can be re-rooted honestly - the whole subchapter nests under it, one level deeper', '`chapter_title_editing` (stays)']
  - ['`tab`', 'the subtree carries NESTED member storage, a blob, or a holder-relative pointer - THE MOVE LAW: the move would copy the projection inline, orphan the directories and rebind the pointers, so it RINGS (a flat member with a clean subtree still moves - the detach)', '[error_flash](*::server:yamlover-editor:error_flash)']
  - ['`tab`', 'otherwise (the root title, or a plain-paragraph neighbour) - Tab never conscripts the previous chunk', '[nop](*::server:yamlover-editor:nop)']
  - ['`shift_tab`', 'a SUBCHAPTER title - the title dissolves back into a plain paragraph (the wrap''s inverse, zero ops when childless): its body splices out after it in order, a keyed description dissolving into an ordinal chunk to move', '[chapter_prose_editing](*::server:chapter-editor:chapter_prose_editing)']
  - ['`shift_tab`', 'the root title', '[nop](*::server:yamlover-editor:nop)']
  - ['`ctrl_alt_number`', '', '[format_switched](*::server:chapter-editor:format_switched)']
  - ['`role_button`', 'T / D on the title/description itself UNMAKES it - the text survives as a plain chunk', '[chapter_prose_editing](*::server:chapter-editor:chapter_prose_editing)']
  - ['`up_down_arrow`', 'one line - both walk to the adjacent editable cell in document order', '`chapter_title_editing` (stays)']
  - ['`backspace`', 'at the START of a subchapter title - joinPrev - THE TITLE DISSOLVES into the preceding paragraph (Tab-wrap''s inverse by deletion); a MATERIALIZED subchapter rings instead', '[chapter_prose_editing](*::server:chapter-editor:chapter_prose_editing)']
  - ['`backspace`', 'the root title, or mid-text - native editing', '`chapter_title_editing` (stays)']
